WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:04.131
In Jobs and Queue, open the existing record for Cluster A.

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:08.440
A pipeline with several Configure actions now identifies each saved

00:00:08.448 --> 00:00:12.877
configuration step. Review its reported stage, timestamps, return

00:00:13.056 --> 00:00:15.855
code, persisted output and diagnostics.

00:00:15.897 --> 00:00:20.454
A failed job shows the last reported or failed stage rather than a misleading

00:00:20.505 --> 00:00:24.977
completed estimate. If no log events or node telemetry were recorded,

00:00:25.156 --> 00:00:27.065
that means evidence is unavailable.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:31.201
It does not prove that Foundation never started or that a later stage

00:00:31.209 --> 00:00:34.998
completed. Use the retained error and the actual target session

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:37.153
to reconcile uncertain state.

00:00:37.353 --> 00:00:40.366
Do not infer success from an aggregate percentage alone.

00:00:40.656 --> 00:00:45.298
The Approvals badge shows an amber pending count or a blue zero when none are
pending.

00:00:45.477 --> 00:00:47.645
An unavailable count is not zero.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:52.251
Open the request and compare its target, exact intent and expiry.

00:00:52.428 --> 00:00:55.620
Sensitive specialist actions require another administrator;

00:00:55.714 --> 00:00:58.138
a changed plan needs renewed approval.

00:00:58.444 --> 00:01:01.948
Test supported automation manually before creating a schedule.

00:01:02.054 --> 00:01:06.441
Parallel execution is appropriate only where the action and independent targets

00:01:06.449 --> 00:01:11.092
support it. It is not a shortcut for concurrent imaging sessions on one Foundation

00:01:11.185 --> 00:01:15.491
VM or for specialist actions that require their own guarded job path.

00:01:15.806 --> 00:01:19.531
A cancellation request cannot undo an accepted remote command.

00:01:19.816 --> 00:01:23.435
Keep the original job and inspect the target before another submission.

00:01:23.656 --> 00:01:27.433
Recovery continuation preserves successful steps and approvals.

00:01:27.641 --> 00:01:32.071
Use its eligible pending-step path rather than restarting the entire pipeline

00:01:32.079 --> 00:01:34.457
to repair a final registration failure.
